nger liner was travelling at 400m/min when the engines were turned off and", "x0": 0.11630980703145652, "y0": 0.7396416573348265, "x1": 0.774253238170764, "y1": 0.7536394176931691}, {"text": "it slowed", "x0": 0.7803330689928628, "y0": 0.7420679357969392, "x1": 0.8530266983875231, "y1": 0.7523329600597238}, {"text": "to 50m/min in 15 minutes, find", "x0": 0.11630980703145652, "y0": 0.7536394176931691, "x1": 0.36849061591329635, "y1": 0.7659574468085106}, {"text": "4 (i) the values of A and k,", "x0": 0.08326724821570182, "y0": 0.7821948488241881, "x1": 0.31297911710282844, "y1": 0.7971257932064203}, {"text": "2 (ii) the speed of the passenger liner 30 minutes after the engines are turned off.", "x0": 0.0816812053925456, "y0": 0.8113101903695409, "x1": 0.7459688078244779, "y1": 0.8258678611422172}], [{"text": "- page 5", "x0": 0.7977795400475813, "y0": 0.03882045539380366, "x1": 0.8612212529738303, "y1": 0.052818215752146326}, {"text": "JRAHS 2 Unit TRIAL HSC 1996", "x0": 0.5088554057626222, "y0": 0.040126913027248974, "x1": 0.7911710282844303, "y1": 0.055617767823814855}, {"text": "QUESTION9: (STARTA NEW PAGE)", "x0": 0.0901401004493788, "y0": 0.060470324748040316, "x1": 0.44065556436690456, "y1": 0.07932064203060843}, {"text": "is the", "x0": 0.7927570711075865, "y0": 0.09014557670772676, "x1": 0.8355802273328047, "y1": 0.10059723777528928}, {"text": "(a) Gas escapes from a damaged container at a rate given by = 1,2t \u2014 360 where V", "x0": 0.09278350515463918, "y0": 0.09089212392683838, "x1": 0.7864128998149617, "y1": 0.11608809257185516}, {"text": "volume, in litres, of gas remaining in the container after t minutes. The container initially", "x0": 0.11842453079566481, "y0": 0.11179544606196341, "x1": 0.8316151202749141, "y1": 0.1351250466592012}, {"text": "held 120000 litres of gas.", "x0": 0.11921755220724294, "y0": 0.1356849570735349, "x1": 0.32646048109965636, "y1": 0.14856289660321015}, {"text": "} @) Find the initial rate of gas leakage.", "x0": 0.08934707903780069, "y0": 0.162187383351997, "x1": 0.42003700766587365, "y1": 0.18271743187756626}, {"text": "Q, (i) Find a formula for the volume of gas remaining in the container after t minutes.", "x0": 0.08855405762622258, "y0": 0.18365061590145576, "x1": 0.7877346021675918, "y1": 0.21071295259425157}, {"text": "2 (iii) Show that the leak is sealed before the container is empty.", "x0": 0.09199048374306107, "y0": 0.21612541993281076, "x1": 0.6225218080888184, "y1": 0.23926838372527062}, {"text": "(b) At a carnival, flags numbered 1, 2 ,3 .4, .... are placed in order along a fun run", "x0": 0.09939201691779011, "y0": 0.2551325121313923, "x1": 0.7774253238170764, "y1": 0.2793952967525196}, {"text": "course.", "x0": 0.7835051546391752, "y0": 0.2560656961552818, "x1": 0.8413957176843775, "y1": 0.2646509891750653}, {"text": "line.", "x0": 0.809674861221253, "y0": 0.26782381485628964, "x1": 0.8437747819191118, "y1": 0.2782754759238522}, {"text": "The flags are placed 125 metres apart with the first flag 350 metres from the starting", "x0": 0.12476870208828972, "y0": 0.26857036207540125, "x1": 0.8041237113402062, "y1": 0.29320642030608435}, {"text": "2. (i) Write a formula for Dp, the distance from the starting line to the nth flag.", "x0": 0.10044937879989427, "y0": 0.2997387084733109, "x1": 0.732751784298176, "y1": 0.32456140350877194}, {"text": "23.", "x0": 0.7980438805181074, "y0": 0.32680104516610675, "x1": 0.8218345228654507, "y1": 0.33725270623366926}, {"text": "4 (ii) Find the distance that a competitor has run if he is standing beside flag number", "x0": 0.10124240021147238, "y0": 0.32792086599477416, "x1": 0.7924927306370605, "y1": 0.35367674505412466}, {"text": "2 (iii) If a girl runs 5 km, which is the nearest flag and how far is she from that flag?", "x0": 0.10573618821041501, "y0": 0.3559163867114595, "x1": 0.7935500925191646, "y1": 0.3818589025755879}, {"text": "QUESTION 10: (START A NEW PAGE)", "x0": 0.1049431667988369, "y0": 0.41974617394550207, "x1": 0.4625958234205657, "y1": 0.4391564016424039}, {"text": "However", "x0": 0.7919640496960084, "y0": 0.4419559537140724, "x1": 0.8670367433254031, "y1": 0.4568868980963046}, {"text": "(a) A company makes 300 chairs per month. At $75 each they can sell all the chairs.", "x0": 0.10652920962199312, "y0": 0.4425158641284061, "x1": 0.7858842188739096, "y1": 0.4678984695782008}, {"text": "a 4 chair", "x0": 0.7850911974623315, "y0": 0.45576707726763716, "x1": 0.8538197197991012, "y1": 0.4665920119447555}, {"text": "the price of each chair can be increased in increments of $3 but this will result in", "x0": 0.13217023526301877, "y0": 0.4570735349010825, "x1": 0.7787470261697066, "y1": 0.48189622993654346}, {"text": "000 per", "x0": 0.802802008987576, "y0": 0.46957820082120194, "x1": 0.8643933386201428, "y1": 0.4824561403508772}, {"text": "reduction in sales for each $3 increment. The company also has fixed costs of $12", "x0": 0.13217023526301877, "y0": 0.4705113848450915, "x1": 0.7972508591065293, "y1": 0.4932810750279955}, {"text": "month.", "x0": 0.13322759714512292, "y0": 0.4970138111235536, "x1": 0.19032513877874702, "y1": 0.507652108995894}, {"text": "by the", "x0": 0.7832408141686492, "y0": 0.5138111235535647, "x1": 0.8324081416864922, "y1": 0.5270623366927958}, {"text": "2 Q) If the number of $3 increments is i, show that the monthly profit $P is given", "x0": 0.0964842717420037, "y0": 0.5147443075774543, "x1": 0.7768966428760243, "y1": 0.544046285927585}, {"text": "formula P = 10500 + 600i \u2014 12i7.", "x0": 0.15675389902194026, "y0": 0.5358342665173572, "x1": 0.44964314036478986, "y1": 0.5541246733855917}, {"text": "profit is", "x0": 0.8215701823949246, "y0": 0.5580440462859276, "x1": 0.8844832143801216, "y1": 0.572415080253826}, {"text": "2, Gi) Find the number of chairs that should be made and their unit price if the monthly", "x0": 0.10811525244514936, "y0": 0.5595371407241508, "x1": 0.8149616706317737, "y1": 0.5862262038073908}, {"text": "to be maximised.", "x0": 0.16441977266719535, "y0": 0.5843598357596118, "x1": 0.3021411578112609, "y1": 0.5968645016797313}, {"text": "(b) A pump delivers a fixed volume of water into a dam at midday each day. The water", "x0": 0.11313772138514407, "y0": 0.6185143710339679, "x1": 0.8146973301612477, "y1": 0.6437103396789847}, {"text": "comes", "x0": 0.8202484800422944, "y0": 0.6188876446435237, "x1": 0.8712661908538197, "y1": 0.6270996640537514}, {"text": "bacteria", "x0": 0.7932857520486386, "y0": 0.6304591265397537, "x1": 0.8567274649748876, "y1": 0.6416573348264277}, {"text": "from a contaminated river and each delivery contains 5000 harmful bacteria. The", "x0": 0.13851440655564368, "y0": 0.6321388577827548, "x1": 0.7879989426381179, "y1": 0.6550951847704367}, {"text": "and", "x0": 0.8546127412106793, "y0": 0.6438969764837627, "x1": 0.8836901929685435, "y1": 0.6543486375513251}, {"text": "once in the dam increase at a rate of 2% per day. Assuming the dam is not contaminated", "x0": 0.1393074279672218, "y0": 0.6448301605076521, "x1": 0.8490615913296325, "y1": 0.6690929451287794}, {"text": "the first delivery is at midday on January Ist,", "x0": 0.1401004493787999, "y0": 0.6648002986188877, "x1": 0.5046259582342056, "y1": 0.6832773422919}, {"text": "| (i) find the number of bacteria in the dam just after midday January 2nd,", "x0": 0.10864393338620143, "y0": 0.6894363568495707, "x1": 0.7213851440655564, "y1": 0.7144456886898096}, {"text": "more than", "x0": 0.796193497224425, "y0": 0.7157521463232549, "x1": 0.8773460216759186, "y1": 0.7265770810003733}, {"text": "9, (ii) show that the number of bacteria in the dam just after midday January 31st is", "x0": 0.10811525244514936, "y0": 0.7168719671519224, "x1": 0.7901136664023262, "y1": 0.7465472191116088}, {"text": "210000.", "x0": 0.16997092254824214, "y0": 0.7426278462112729, "x1": 0.2373777425323817, "y1": 0.7536394176931691}, {"text": "be the", "x0": 0.8009516256938938, "y0": 0.7584919746173946, "x1": 0.8493259318001586, "y1": 0.76931690929